  "brief": {
    "story": "The client’s spec, in words: “the siren sounds when the alarm is armed and the door or the window is open.” That’s ARM AND (DOOR OR WINDOW): a 74HC32 for the OR and a 74HC08 for the AND. Both chips are wired except the link between them.",
    "goal": "Wire the OR gate’s output into the AND gate so SIREN = ARM AND (DOOR OR WINDOW).",
    "datasheet": {
      "title": "Two chips",
      "rows": [
        [
          "IC1 74HC32",
          "DOOR, WINDOW → pin 3 (column 5)"
        ],
        [
          "IC2 74HC08",
          "pins 1 (column 17), 2 (ARM) → 3"
        ],
        [
          "SIREN",
          "from IC2 pin 3"
        ]
      ]
    }
  },
  "hints": [
    "Split the sentence at the AND: one input is ARM, the other is “door or window”, which IC1 already makes on its pin 3.",
    "IC1’s pin 3 is column 5. IC2’s free input, pin 1, is column 17.",
    "A wire from column 5 to column 17."
  ],
